id: pm-n8a6e7
title: "pm search defaults to keyword on a workspace whose vector index is complete, so the shipped Ollama semantic default never reaches the default query path"
description: "Measured 2026-09-08 on the live 2719-item workspace. The vectorization ledger (search/vectorization-status.json) reports 2719 of 2719 items embedded with provider ollama, model qwen3-embedding:0.6b, 1024 dimensions, and pm health reports vectorization ok. Yet a bare pm search (the form every skill, AGENTS.md quickstart line and the generated agent-guidance block instruct, 21 fenced occurrences, 0 of them naming a mode) runs in keyword mode: the top result for \"make command output cheaper in tokens for coding agents\" is the roadmap hub pm-doxj (score 5399) followed by the context-engine hub pm-4k6b, while --mode hybrid returns pm-t5dt4z, pm-kvxqp1 and pm-5t33or (the three items that actually own output token cost) in 1.3 seconds. The cold-start duplicate check every agent performs therefore runs against the weakest retrieval the workspace has.\n\nThree layers agree on the literal and none consults index state: parseSearchMode(undefined) returns \"keyword\" in src/sdk/query/search-contracts.ts, the CLI re-derives the same literal in src/cli/register-list-query.ts (mode fallback \"keyword\", help text \"default: keyword\"), and settings.search has no key for a default mode at all, so no workspace can change it without passing --mode on every call. pm-67uh closed on 2026-05 with the acceptance criterion \"When Ollama is available locally, default pm search mode resolves to semantic-capable hybrid behavior with no manual setup; explicit user settings still take precedence\". The shipped runtime defaults (semantic-defaults.ts) fill provider, model and vector-store leaves, which is why the index exists, but the mode default itself never moved. The SDK already degrades any semantic failure to keyword hits with a search_semantic_fallback warning, so an index-aware hybrid default cannot block an agent when Ollama is down.\n\nExpected: the default mode is an SDK policy resolved from workspace state and settings, not a presentation-layer literal. A settings key search.default_mode accepts auto, keyword, semantic or hybrid with default auto; auto resolves to hybrid exactly when the built-in semantic path can run (an active embedding provider plus an active vector store or extension adapter, or an extension search provider) and to keyword otherwise; the response reports mode_source (explicit, settings or auto) so the reader can tell a chosen mode from a derived one; the CLI passes mode through unchanged and its help text says auto; docs and the config key registry declare the key."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,recurrence,sdk-first,search,semantic
created_at: "2026-09-08T13:02:28.189Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T14:39:46.770Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T14:21:47.777Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T14:21:47.777Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "search.default_mode is a declared settings key (auto|keyword|semantic|hybrid, default auto) accepted by the validator, the nested config registry and pm config set; With auto, a workspace whose stored search.provider names the active embedding provider and whose vector store resolves runs bare pm search in hybrid mode, and a workspace without that configuration runs keyword, proven by specs in both directions; Verbose search responses always report mode_source (explicit, settings or auto); compact responses report it only when settings pinned the mode; the CLI no longer re-derives the default from a literal; pm search --help and docs/COMMANDS.md and docs/CONFIGURATION.md describe the auto default and the key, and the contracts snapshot, intent calibration ledger and recurrence policy are regenerated or registered; A bare pm search on this workspace returns the semantic ranking for the measured query and the semantic fallback warning still appears when the provider is unreachable"
parent: pm-ydp6
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "search-contracts.ts owns SearchDefaultMode, SearchModeSource and resolveEffectiveSearchMode; search.ts resolves the runtime mode from the health-consistent configured verdict; search.default_mode declared in types, defaults, validator, serializer and config registry; CLI literal removed; verbose responses carry mode_source, compact only for settings; docs, contracts snapshot, calibration ledger, recurrence family, SDK surface snapshot updated"
expected_result: "Bare pm search uses the strongest retrieval the workspace can run, chosen by the SDK from configured provider and store state, with the choice visible in verbose responses and pinnable through settings"
actual_result: "On this workspace a bare pm search reports mode hybrid with the semantic ranking (pm-t5dt4z, pm-kvxqp1, pm-5t33or, pm-cu1i for the measured query); explicit --mode keyword reports mode_source explicit; a workspace without a configured provider stays keyword and never contacts a provider; a failing provider degrades to keyword hits with the fallback warning"
