comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T13:02:40.492Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before filing: hybrid searches for 'pm search defaults to keyword mode even though semantic index exists' and 'search mode selection policy declared in settings hybrid default' returned only closed lineage (pm-wn3r, pm-67uh, pm-75k9, pm-2xwh, pm-qyyv) and no open owner; pm-28cf (provider string normalization), pm-p1g43q (retrieval quality contract) and pm-vjgqj5 (Ollama batch ceiling) own adjacent but distinct defects. Verified facts: parseSearchMode(undefined) returns keyword in src/sdk/query/search-contracts.ts line 72; src/cli/register-list-query.ts line 692 re-derives the keyword literal and line 1357 prints default keyword; settings.search declares no mode key (src/core/shared/constants.ts line 314); vectorization-status.json reports 2719 embedded, ollama, qwen3-embedding:0.6b, 1024 dims."
  "2026-09-08T13:38:52.411Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence 2026-09-08. SDK: search-contracts.ts gains SearchDefaultMode, SEARCH_DEFAULT_MODE_VALUES, SearchModeSource, resolveSearchDefaultModeSetting and resolveEffectiveSearchMode; search.ts resolves the runtime mode through resolveRuntimeSearchMode, which counts the semantic path as runnable only when resolveProviderConfigSource (the predicate pm health publishes as provider_source) returns configured for the stored search.provider and a vector store or extension adapter resolves, or an extension search provider is active. Settings: search.default_mode (default auto) declared in types, defaults, validator, serializer key order and the nested config registry as search_default_mode. CLI: the keyword literal and its help text are gone; help says default auto. Live on this workspace after the change: bare search mode hybrid, top hits pm-t5dt4z, pm-kvxqp1, pm-5t33or, pm-cu1i (was pm-doxj, pm-4k6b, pm-rnpb, pm-92if); explicit --mode keyword reports mode_source explicit; count-only under auto reports 666 hybrid matches versus 946 keyword. Golden set (pm eval --k 10): hybrid nDCG 0.8244 / MRR 0.90 / recall 0.8364, keyword 0.7451 / 0.80 / 0.8727, semantic 0.7890 / 0.85 / 0.8182. Gate repairs the change required: recurrence family presentation-layer-default-re-derivation registered so the recurs_from edge passes the defect-evidence gate; intent calibration ledger re-approved (+21 bytes of mode_source in the unbounded verbose walk); help text kept at the previous token length because the lexicon ratchet has zero headroom; compact responses omit mode_source for explicit and auto after the agent-task token ratchet showed six tokens per search for a fact the default already states. Targeted specs: 100 of 100 across search-command and search-default-mode, 188 across the settings, constants, alias and nested-settings suites."
  "2026-09-08T13:49:26.557Z","harness:claude-code","SDK surface: the snapshot gate classified the optional default_mode key on PmSettings.search as a signature change on ./sdk, ./sdk/core and ./sdk/runtime and refused a silent update; acknowledged with a recorded reason (existing settings literals stay valid, readers normalize an absent key to auto) alongside four additive exports: SearchDefaultMode, SearchModeResolution, SearchModeSource and resolveEffectiveSearchMode on ./sdk and ./sdk/query."
  "2026-09-08T14:03:18.664Z","harness:claude-code","Graph-composition gate: the seven related rows first written for the duplicate-check neighbours pushed the assurance related count to 6060 against its 6053 ceiling (the ceiling is denominated in declared rows, where pm graph audit reports 5570 deduplicated), so they were withdrawn; the citation holders pm-n8a6e7 and pm-2ksptv are exempted from the prose-edge-gaps measure with recorded reasons in the same shape as the pm-7zs0 exemption, and pm-p1g43q now carries blocked_by pm-n8a6e7 because its bare-search recall targets depend on the default mode being settled SDK policy. Dry-run verdict after the change: pass, prose-edge-gaps 1342 of 1343, related 6053 of 6053."
  "2026-09-08T14:39:46.770Z","harness:claude-code","Hosted coverage on 1773623ed reported 99.99 percent statements and branches: search-contracts.ts line 72 (the raw parser's undefined fallback, unreachable from the runtime after the CLI stopped passing an absent mode) and search.ts line 2854 (the extension-vector-adapter side of the auto rule). Added a parser unit test and an extension-adapter auto-to-hybrid scenario; scoped coverage of both files reports no uncovered line in the new code."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T13:34:35.247Z","harness:claude-code","A closed feature's acceptance criterion is a claim the current build must still keep. pm-67uh closed in May on \"default pm search mode resolves to hybrid when Ollama is available\", and by September three layers agreed on a keyword literal (SDK parse default, CLI fallback, no settings key) with every test green, because no test executed the criterion against the runtime. Re-execute the AC of the closed item that owns a behaviour before trusting the behaviour."
  "2026-09-08T13:34:35.867Z","harness:claude-code","An index-aware default must key off the same verdict the diagnostics already publish, not off whether defaults were applied. The first cut of auto treated auto_ollama_defaults_applied as \"implicit\" and resolved keyword on this very workspace, because one mirror leaf (search.embedding_model) was empty and the defaults filler touched it. resolveProviderConfigSource, the function pm health uses for provider_source, is the honest predicate: configured when the stored search.provider names the active provider."
  "2026-09-08T13:34:36.523Z","harness:claude-code","Three gates react to a one-line output change and each has its own sanctioned repair: a recurs_from edge is refused by the defect-evidence gate until the lineage is registered as a family in config/defect-recurrence-policy.json; the intent calibration ledger is a byte ratchet that needs pnpm context:intent:calibrate --update plus a reviewed diff (here 21 bytes of mode_source, one fewer compacted row at tier 1); the help-token budget has zero headroom per command, so new help text must be no longer than what it replaces (default: auto) or the ceiling must be raised with a dated comment."
